  "entry_after": {
    "id": "M21",
    "title_zh": "知识与生活：相连的哲学候选",
    "title_en": "Knowing and living: connected philosophical proposal",
    "claim_zh": "认识、纠正与模型修订构成相连候选。G0下意识分化生的意义，新的生也可有正面意义且不自动产生特定义务。保存已有生活能够要求实际更新；更强争点是超出既有请求与保存目标的新实现。整体改名不能隐去毁损，拒绝福利性创造理由不等于否定全部生成根据。",
    "claim_en": "Knowing, correction and model revision form a connected account. Under G0, consciousness differentiates living significance and new living can count positively without assigning a specific duty. Preservation can require renewal; the sharper dispute concerns new realization beyond incumbent claims and preservation targets. Redescription cannot erase destruction, and rejecting a welfare-based creation reason does not reject every generative ground.",
    "scope_zh": "两个范围问题在G0/J下的完成保留；扩读Frick的接续价值论，新增Finneron-Burns原典检验保存对象的界定，纠正过粗的对手归类。无新定理、实验或独立验收；整套理论必要性、最广组织范围及普遍意识／语义仍未证。继承界面相容8／11、一般相容13／18、模型修订30／72及76次执行、来源26／53、选择性修订16／32与四项统计复核原范围；完成的实践与对齐方向不重开。",
    "scope_en": "The two G0/J scope answers remain complete. Extended Frick reading and a new Finneron-Burns comparison sharpen the preservation target and correct an overly broad rival classification. No new theorem, experiment or independent acceptance. Whole-theory necessity, the broadest organizational scope and universal consciousness/semantics remain unproved. Inherited profile compatibility 8/11, general compatibility 13/18, model revision 30/72 and 76 runs, source reliance 26/53, selective revision 16/32 and four-statistic checks retain their scopes; completed practical and alignment arguments are reused.",
